// What a function's row says about the code a case cannot see into: 0 for an
// ordinary function, 1 for a body the digest cannot see and whose result may
// differ between runs (a native that is not file-pure, or a function whose
// tokens were never recorded -- only a hand-built fixture's), 2 for a native
// named in cache_file_natives or cache_taint_natives (compiler/parse/conf.id),
// whose backend logs what it reads or marks the case when it does something
// else. dg_seal (../../../scc/seal/) folds the classes of everything a
// component reaches together with `|`, so a case's dirt is 0, 2 (key it, and
// record the files it reads) or has bit 1 (never key it).
dg_nat_class(int dgf, string dgnm) {
  int dgc = 0;
  if(dgf >= len((import ptoke))) {
    dgc = 1;
  } else if(is_native((import prog)[dgf]) == 1) {
    dgc = 1;
    if(list_string_index((import cache_file_natives), dgnm) >= 0 || list_string_index((import cache_taint_natives), dgnm) >= 0) {
      dgc = 2;
    }
  }
} return int dgc;
